            "id": 3261,
            "sort": 1,
            "name": "Introduction",
            "value": "<p>It has been observed that numerous animal species are facing extinction as a result of human activities occurring both on land and in the ocean. This alarming trend can be attributed to several factors, and timely action is necessary to address this pressing issue.</p>",
            "question_id": 42030,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 3262,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p><strong>Human activities are the primary causes behind the declining populations of various animal species. </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(45, 194, 107);\">Firstly, poaching and overhunting for profit remain significant threats to wildlife. An example of this would be the rhinoceros, which is often hunted for its horn in order to make so-called \"miracle medicine,\" thus causing the species to become critically endangered. In addition, elephants are also targeted for their ivory tusks, which are sold on the black market for enormous profits. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(53, 152, 219);\">Secondly, industrial pollution has severely damaged natural ecosystems. Factories frequently dump toxic chemicals into rivers and oceans, which poisons marine animals and renders their habitats unlivable. As a consequence, many aquatic species such as fish and sea turtles struggle to survive in such contaminated environments.</span></p>",
            "question_id": 42030,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 3263,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"JuQideLPRoMGEExA9v7lN5ifg4d\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-KpsldoIanoFGZWxFRQtlF21igte\"><strong>However, I believe there are several measures that can be implemented to mitigate these problems.</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(45, 194, 107);\">One solution would be for authorities to impose stricter laws and heavier penalties for those who engage in poaching and illegal hunting. Such measures would deter potential poachers from targeting protected species, and in order to ensure that offenders are caught and punished, more funding for guards and rangers patrolling natural habitats is urgently necessary.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(53, 152, 219);\">Another solution is for governments to enforce tighter regulations on industrial waste and emissions, such as requiring factories to install waste treatment systems and imposing heavy fines on businesses that violate these rules. By doing so, companies would be discouraged from dumping toxic substances into the environment, which would allow animal populations to gradually recover in cleaner ecosystems.</span></div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 42030,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 3264,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Conclusion",
            "value": "<p>In conclusion, poaching driven by profit and pollution caused by industrial activities are the main reasons behind the extinction of many species. To tackle this issue, governments must take decisive action by cracking down on illegal hunting and implementing stricter controls on factory emissions.</p>",
